        "title": "Sexual Selection and Life History Theory",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Sexual selection is selection arising from differential mating success, not differential\nsurvival. It drives the evolution of ornaments, weapons, and mate preferences — often\nproducing traits that reduce survival but increase reproduction."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-SEXUAL-SELECTION.md#003",
      "path": [
        "07-SEXUAL-SELECTION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:evolutionary-biology:07-sexual-selection, git-history:evolutionary-biology:07-sexual-selection]",
        "canonical_path": "evolutionary-biology/07-SEXUAL-SELECTION.md",
        "concepts": "[sexual, selection]",
        "current_path": "evolutionary-biology/07-SEXUAL-SELECTION.md",
        "id": "maxim:evolutionary-biology:sexual-selection",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "evolutionary-biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[sexual, selection]",
        "section": "evolutionary-biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Sexual Selection and Life History Theory",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│               SEXUAL SELECTION FRAMEWORK                         │\n│                                                                  │\n│  SEXUAL SELECTION                  NATURAL SELECTION             │\n│  ────────────────                  ──────────────────            │\n│  Currency: mating success          Currency: survival + reprod.  │\n│  Often sex-limited expression      Acts on both sexes            │\n│  Can oppose natural selection      Generally adaptive            │\n│  Produces costly ornaments         Eliminates costly traits      │\n│                                                                  │\n│  MECHANISMS:                                                     │\n│  ─────────────                                                   │\n│  Intrasexual: male-male competition → weapons (antlers, fangs)   │\n│  Intersexual: female choice → ornaments (peacock tail, song)     │\n│               Mutual choice: both sexes choose (monogamous spp.) │\n│                                                                  │\n│  WHY ORNAMENTS ARE HONEST SIGNALS:                               │\n│  Runaway selection (Fisher)   vs.   Handicap principle (Zahavi)  │\n│  → Arbitrary but self-        →  Signal is costly and            │\n│    reinforcing preference         condition-dependent:           │\n│    + trait coupling               only high-quality males can    │\n│                                   afford it                      │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```"
    },
    {
