        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "### Fisherian Runaway"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-SEXUAL-SELECTION.md#013",
      "path": [
        "07-SEXUAL-SELECTION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:evolutionary-biology:07-sexual-selection, git-history:evolutionary-biology:07-sexual-selection]",
        "canonical_path": "evolutionary-biology/07-SEXUAL-SELECTION.md",
        "concepts": "[sexual, selection]",
        "current_path": "evolutionary-biology/07-SEXUAL-SELECTION.md",
        "id": "maxim:evolutionary-biology:sexual-selection",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "evolutionary-biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[sexual, selection]",
        "section": "evolutionary-biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Sexual Selection and Life History Theory",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Fisher (1930) proposed that female preferences and male ornaments can co-evolve in\na positive feedback loop:"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-SEXUAL-SELECTION.md#014",
      "path": [
        "07-SEXUAL-SELECTION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:evolutionary-biology:07-sexual-selection, git-history:evolutionary-biology:07-sexual-selection]",
        "canonical_path": "evolutionary-biology/07-SEXUAL-SELECTION.md",
        "concepts": "[sexual, selection]",
        "current_path": "evolutionary-biology/07-SEXUAL-SELECTION.md",
        "id": "maxim:evolutionary-biology:sexual-selection",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "evolutionary-biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[sexual, selection]",
        "section": "evolutionary-biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Sexual Selection and Life History Theory",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  Initial state: female preference for slightly longer tails\n                 (arbitrary or from weak natural selection on tail)\n                          ↓\n  Generation 1:  females with preference mate with long-tailed males\n                 Sons: inherit long tails\n                 Daughters: inherit preference for long tails\n                          ↓\n  Subsequent:    Alleles for \"preference\" and \"long tail\" become genetically\n                 correlated (linkage disequilibrium at the phenotypic level)\n                          ↓\n  Runaway:       As preference becomes common, long-tailed males have higher\n                 mating success even if slightly less viable\n                 Selection for ornament accelerates\n                          ↓\n  Equilibrium:   Natural selection against the ornament eventually balances\n                 (or the ornament becomes so extreme it causes extinction)\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-SEXUAL-SELECTION.md#015",
      "path": [
        "07-SEXUAL-SELECTION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:evolutionary-biology:07-sexual-selection, git-history:evolutionary-biology:07-sexual-selection]",
        "canonical_path": "evolutionary-biology/07-SEXUAL-SELECTION.md",
        "concepts": "[sexual, selection]",
        "current_path": "evolutionary-biology/07-SEXUAL-SELECTION.md",
        "id": "maxim:evolutionary-biology:sexual-selection",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "evolutionary-biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[sexual, selection]",
        "section": "evolutionary-biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Sexual Selection and Life History Theory",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The model: a genetic correlation between \"choosiness\" alleles and \"ornament\" alleles.\nThe feedback loop is self-reinforcing — \"arbitrary\" preferences can evolve and produce\nelaborated traits purely from internal evolutionary dynamics."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-SEXUAL-SELECTION.md#016",
      "path": [
