      "text": "CRYPTIC FEMALE CHOICE:\n  ──────────────────────\n  Females can bias fertilization success after mating (mechanism not always clear):\n  - Selective reabsorption of sperm from different males\n  - Differential use of stored sperm\n  - Immunological biases (MHC-dissimilar sperm preferentially used in some species)\n  MHC-based mate choice: T-shirt experiment (Wedekind 1995) — women rate\n  odors of MHC-dissimilar men as more attractive. May function to produce\n  MHC-heterozygous offspring with broader immune repertoire.\n```"
